{title: Ziklag}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 27:2; 27:5–6; 27:7–12}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He crossed the border [Gm7]with six hundred men
[C]To Achish son of Maoch, king of [Dm]Gath
David asked for favor in [Gm7]the eyes
[C]A place in one of the out[Dm]lying towns
[Bb]Why live in the royal c[Dm]ity with you?
[Bb]Your servant asks for a small [A]place to stay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]That day Achish gave him [Gm7]Ziklag
Ziklag belongs to the [C]kings of Judah [Dm]
A year and four months in Philis[Gm7]tine land
Living in [Bb]the shadow of [A7]a foreign [Dm]crown
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
David and his men [Gm7]went up to raid
The [C]Geshurites, the Girzites, Amale[Dm]kites
They took sheep, cattle, donkeys, camels
[Gm7]No man or woman left alive behind
[Bb]He returned to [A7]Achish with the [Dm]spoils
[Bb]Saying he raided the Ne[Dm]gev of Judah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
That day Achish gave him [Gm7]Ziklag
Ziklag belongs to the [C]kings of Judah [Dm]
A year and four months in Philis[Gm7]tine land
Living in [Bb]the shadow of [A7]a foreign [Dm]crown
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Achish trusted him, thinking [Gm7]he was detestable
[C]Made himself utterly loathsome [Dm]to Israel
He thought David would be [Gm7]his servant for life
[Bb]Deceiving [A7]the king with every [Dm]report
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]David left no one to report [Dm]his deeds
[Bb]Such was his practice the whole [Dm]time he lived
In the [Bb]territory of the son of Maac[Dm]ah
[Bb]Hiding his true [A7]path from the [Dm]eyes of Gath
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Ziklag has belonged to [A7]the kings of Judah
To this [Dm]day
{end_of_verse}
